   "value": "Thirty-two treatment-seeking, nicotine-dependent smokers viewed blocks of smoking-related and neutral cues alternating with rest during fMRI. They completed back-to-back scans under instructions to allow themselves to crave and then to resist the urge to smoke. The study used a block design and analyzed smoking-related cues versus neutral cues, craving versus resisting, and resistance-strategy comparisons.",
   "value_source": "generated"
